e","title":"value"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The elision type represents an elision between lyric syllables. The text content specifies the symbol used to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display the elision. Common values are a no-break space (Unicode 00A0), an underscore (Unicode 005F), or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undertie (Unicode 203F). If the text content is empty, the smufl attribute is used to specify the symbol to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use. Its value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics. The SMuFL attribute is ignored if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elision glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor a smufl attribute are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present, the elision glyph is application-specific."}],"title":"MXLElision","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision"}}}